## 3. Exact kernel certificate

Let

\[
M_{12}^{\mathrm{red}}\in K^{1324\times956}
\]

be the exact G3EC matrix. G3EJ emits ten vectors

\[
v_1,\ldots,v_{10}\in K^{956}.
\]

Every coordinate is represented in the power basis
\(1,\gamma,\ldots,\gamma^5\). Direct coefficient arithmetic modulo the defining
minimal polynomial gives

\[
M_{12}^{\mathrm{red}}v_i=0
\qquad (1\le i\le10).
\]

The independent verifier checks all

\[
1324\cdot10=13240
\]

residual slots and finds zero nonzero coefficients. The emitted vector
coefficients have bit lengths between 127 and 164, so the certificate is a
literal exact basis rather than a high-precision approximation.

The selected reduction has ten free component-12 columns, numbered 531 through
540 in zero-based reduced coordinates. Projection of the ten vectors to those
columns gives a \(10\times10\) matrix. Its determinant satisfies

\[
\det P\equiv1071\not\equiv0
\pmod{(21817,\gamma-5)}.
\]

Therefore \(\det P\ne0\) in \(K\), and the ten exact kernel vectors are
\(K\)-independent. Their component-12 source projections are independent as
well.

## 4. Exact rank squeeze

The same reduced matrix has rank 946 at the good reduction
\((21817,\gamma-5)\). Reduction cannot increase rank, hence

\[
\operatorname{rank}_K M_{12}^{\mathrm{red}}\ge946.
\]

Ten independent exact kernel vectors in a 956-column matrix give

\[
\operatorname{rank}_K M_{12}^{\mathrm{red}}\le956-10=946.
\]

The bounds meet:

\[
\boxed{\operatorname{rank}_K M_{12}^{\mathrm{red}}=946,
\qquad\dim_K\ker M_{12}^{\mathrm{red}}=10.}
\]

G3EC obtained this matrix from the 2,113-column post-G3DZ presentation by
1,157 exact unit-pivot contractions. Reversing them preserves nullity and adds
one rank per pivot. Thus the original presentation has

\[
\operatorname{rank}_K M_{12}=946+1157=2103,
\qquad\dim_K\ker M_{12}=10.
\]

The 81-dimensional new source block therefore has exact rank increment

\[
\boxed{\Delta r_{12}=81-10=71.}
\]

